{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuirsgTQ3TRQYLtgJYHe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't find `createAISDKTelemetry()` anywhere: not in Cloudflare's docs, not in any search result, and not in this directory. Cloudflare's [agent tracing changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-08-04-agent-tracing/) instead documents **`wrapAISDK()`** from `agents/observability/ai`, so `createAISDKTelemetry` is probably an old or wrong name. Check the `agents` package exports before relying on it.\n\nThe documented setup has two steps:\n1. Turn on Workers traces in your Wrangler config. I believe the setting is `\"observability\": { \"traces\": { \"enabled\": true } }`.\n2. Wrap the AI SDK namespace once and call the AI SDK functions through the wrapped copy. The changelog says this supports AI SDK v6 and v7.\n\nI haven't run this; the import path and \"wrap the namespace once\" come from the changelog, and the exact call shape is my reading of it:\n\n```ts\nimport * as ai from \"ai\";\nimport { wrapAISDK } from \"agents/observability/ai\";\n\nconst { generateText, streamText } = wrapAISDK(ai);\n```\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare changelog – Agent tracing (2026-08-04)](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-08-04-agent-tracing/)\n- [Cloudflare blog – Agent Development Lifecycle / tracing](https://blog.cloudflare.com/tag/tracing/)\n- [Flowith – Cloudflare agent tracing with OpenTelemetry & AI SDK](https://flowith.io/blog/cloudflare-agent-tracing-opentelemetry-ai-sdk-guide/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":22425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1122},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pa